  "review_scope": "Read all 21 proof blocks and checked their original contracts, including unrestricted BiValue, all four MtoHM fields, standard coordinates, complete_rows and every-h1 block_of_normal_form. The final actual row window retains the original supplied MConcl. No whole global closure follows.",
  "claims_reviewed": [
    {
      "id": "DJW1",
      "block_sha256": "947fc693177ed667e20793898296b23258b61a72f9b9317ac7d442a213610cd9",
      "result": "PASS",
      "mathematical_review": "Bezout identifies the integer valuation without discreteness; Legendre and digit sums give both factorial bounds, including zero multiindices."
    },
    {
      "id": "DJW2",
      "block_sha256": "f85bf3e7cd4315c22f7c69b469f45ec222817de8d9c08be478f44612dd1f4c27",
      "result": "PASS",
      "mathematical_review": "Ordinary Cayley, explicitly retained as a classical identity, iterates to C_r(m). Moving multiplication through the factorial pairing gives the stated ratio with nonzero denominators."
    },
    {
      "id": "DJW3",
      "block_sha256": "245d7396e91785b8c2052f7846c65df342b3c36216e110766ca65355991bc0e3",
      "result": "PASS",
      "mathematical_review": "The positive Y-degree makes every exponential coefficient finite. Valuation of t! is offset by the weighted lower bound. Frobenius modulo p and the number of positive Z-degree factors give the exact divisibility and degree of Psi^s."
    },
    {
      "id": "DJW4",
      "block_sha256": "3542e45a541c1e41e059b66b421705ab69504a94dfa27322b6eedc34453d0946",
      "result": "PASS",
      "mathematical_review": "Conjugation of finite ordinary differential operators and the Cayley adjoint formula give an exact finite Newton expansion for each y; a_0=1 is justified by E(X,0)=1."
    },
    {
      "id": "DJW5",
      "block_sha256": "ff7f8d60f974b9af6a50ad2b592c5cf4aea054b19f48f1624da520281c98c0b2",
      "result": "PASS",
      "mathematical_review": "The two factorial normalizations, weighted coefficient bound, Psi divisibility and e identity yield the stated s/8 bound with the full logarithmic loss; no asymptotic coefficient is substituted for a finite one."
    },
    {
      "id": "DJW6",
      "block_sha256": "e4e5034b1a797728d8d40e9e73e6b233fac5cb770c9635933caa70896087b317",
      "result": "PASS",
      "mathematical_review": "The explicit ceiling threshold and logarithmic inequalities imply strict positivity for every s at or beyond S, with all p>=5, odd h>=1 and r>=1 retained."
    },
    {
      "id": "DJW7",
      "block_sha256": "1442d138d22e00f776a8071d32c146a7c0f48bdc1975952e8ff396b4a8248339",
      "result": "PASS",
      "mathematical_review": "The translated binomial evaluation matrix has determinant one and an integer inverse; this works for every translated interval and does not require large residue characteristic."
    },
    {
      "id": "DJW8",
      "block_sha256": "c24d1c3af19dddc24c2e40e75061e12f9d3292529b2c22ab9f4eab56e67064cd",
      "result": "PASS",
      "mathematical_review": "Tail coefficients are strictly positive in valuation and the integer interpolation recovers a_0=1, forcing one good y. The returned original bound and the separate empty-matrix case match full ThmP."
    },
    {
      "id": "DJW9",
      "block_sha256": "bc3792b5bdbf9949fb803f551a320b30e27ac7a29f360fb84149e657846a9346",
      "result": "PASS",
      "mathematical_review": "Restriction of the source mvExp is proved coefficientwise with its finite degree truncation even for nonzero constant term; use of the genuine exponential is confined to zero constant term."
    },
    {
      "id": "DJW10",
      "block_sha256": "83244dcab6eb8ea02120a95ce147390496fc8c474e4e2d81cc583de1a696fb4f",
      "result": "PASS",
      "mathematical_review": "Determinant permutation expansions force the prescribed diagonal rows and the complementary block; the argument is over arbitrary commutative coefficient rings."
    },
    {
      "id": "DJW11",
      "block_sha256": "6c3d45d960cc4db5c63dabaaffb960db4f0ecdb7bf46a07ac5faee470eba9697",
      "result": "PASS",
      "mathematical_review": "Multigraded minimal degrees eliminate all higher coordinate and row-exponential terms in the extra rows. Ordinary derivatives yield exactly ((A! B!))^(n-r), including zero exponents."
    },
    {
      "id": "DJW12",
      "block_sha256": "4dfc7d211e2bac80a18ceed50f8126599030474a89f3cd14a151fa1e7439fb09",
      "result": "PASS",
      "mathematical_review": "All BiHyp fields are used at their literal scope. The proof preserves arbitrary l,i,n,r,y, including l=0/i=0/n=0, and does not import the valuation or oddness assumptions from ThmP."
    },
    {
      "id": "DJW13",
      "block_sha256": "dcef9beb3eeb3f128799f67e28dc031ea53d1aca2cd6f8c4b3091c9752278c2b",
      "result": "PASS",
      "mathematical_review": "The factorial valuations and monotonicity of the nonnegative slope provide the literal BiContent bound with the original r,n distinction."
    },
    {
      "id": "DJW14",
      "block_sha256": "06e55dbd50921dadc5a81b0b0ec85af565412d6b89a3f67fdcb0432e1c2f3d46",
      "result": "PASS",
      "mathematical_review": "The exact BiValue identity followed by ThmP and the factorial content bound proves BiWindow with its original rank-defect hypothesis and window length."
    },
    {
      "id": "DJW15",
      "block_sha256": "001b1b99e3cfac421e67c9b5cc8076a95c90c6ad4fb280695a4f5cad2d3b1e31",
      "result": "PASS",
      "mathematical_review": "The original MConcl weighted remainder and axis vanishing give HM1/HM2 on the actual restricted series. Row separation and the optional level-one low-degree clause supply all four MtoHM fields."
    },
    {
      "id": "DJW16",
      "block_sha256": "0a832aed4983e8d5a9c5dabf3bde9081e0697436abb263ba62f291ca86da3af4",
      "result": "PASS",
      "mathematical_review": "A nonzero kernel vector can be normalized at one minimum-valued coordinate without a discrete valuation. The appended row and column preserve both splittings and integrality at every intermediate size, hence give an integral square unit."
    },
    {
      "id": "DJW17",
      "block_sha256": "b31ece2460a41a094419a75ce2d913ec0cae1c0138897e5768a7031f585b617c",
      "result": "PASS",
      "mathematical_review": "The original Cart existence axiom supplies typed curves with standard initial vectors; coefficientwise contraction of the order-two correction gives actual standard coordinates and the required uniqueness."
    },
    {
      "id": "DJW18",
      "block_sha256": "0a90f7021f570ffcb5d5b7bd38a01f6483e461a3cb4867cece490e83581a6d83",
      "result": "PASS",
      "mathematical_review": "The ordinary chain rule for linear substitution is checked on monomials and factorials. The determinant factor has the displayed direction, rather than an inverse or a divided-power normalization."
    },
    {
      "id": "DJW19",
      "block_sha256": "719d113bfd25b0e14de09f14397fb43ff5daea0589ca535faf2c6449cbdc46dc",
      "result": "PASS",
      "mathematical_review": "The completed integral Abar and integral inverse of Y supply the actual row substitutions and diagonal-coordinate first jets. The restricted original gauge equals the exact supplied main-term expression before y is chosen."
    },
    {
      "id": "DJW20",
      "block_sha256": "c059989b251d3c02f903063a9b78d5a4cfacf6b6595923b1f06f8227fa3c6957",
      "result": "PASS",
      "mathematical_review": "The polynomial gamma has integral coefficients and its substitution by the fixed coordinates is literally IntGerm. The derivative change gives det(Abar)^(qy) det(Y)^y; both are units, yielding equality of valuations. Arbitrary supplied h1 with the original restriction identity remains allowed."
    },
    {
      "id": "DJW21",
      "block_sha256": "b5d04e8237fa537628874900a9125e2561e4f8ab97a4ff823218857c04911fe5",
      "result": "PASS",
      "mathematical_review": "The rank-defect inequality and monotonicity of S install the exact original Windows bound with one coordinate choice before every window origin. The r=0 and y=0 cases are explicit. LemmaM existence and the global theta family remain retained producers."
    }
